// Block-world textures (Minecraft-style, Minetest Game CC BY-SA 3.0 + others, see gen/tex/CREDITS_textures.md)
// Each PNG is 64x64 (16x16 source pixels upscaled 4x nearest, or 32x32 upscaled 2x).
// XScale/YScale 2.0 -> one texture = 32x32 map units = one block (the 56-unit player is 1.75 blocks tall).
// WorldPanning: sidedef/flat offsets stay in map units, so Doom's 8/16/32/64 alignments still line up.
// The doors (64x128 PNG) are 32x64 map units: a two-block Minecraft door.

Texture "MCGRASS", 64, 64
{
	XScale 2.0
	YScale 2.0
	WorldPanning
	Patch "textures/blocks/b_grass.png", 0, 0
}
